 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 521059,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/b0bfcb9de0204c3d.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n(credit: modification of work by Rix I, Nexøe-Larsen C, Bergmann NC, et al./MDText.com, Inc., CC-BY-NC-ND)\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>Glucagon is a hormone that plays a role in controlling blood glucose. The graphs show the blood glucose concentration and glucagon concentration in different scenarios. Hyperglycemia is having too much glucose, euglycemia is having normal amounts of it and hypoglycemia is having too little glucose in blood.</p>\n<p>Based on this data, what is the role of glucagon?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1018545,
     "content_html": "Trigger the processes that change glucose to other molecules."
    },
    {
     "id": 1018546,
     "content_html": "Trigger the processes that change other molecules to glucose."
    },
    {
     "id": 1018547,
     "content_html": "Trigger the processes that get cells to use up more energy."
    },
    {
     "id": 1018548,
     "content_html": "Trigger the processes that get cells to use up less energy."
    }
   ],
